{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families","id":1164481,"title":"Do sin-eaters usually go back to their families?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-02T01:39:47-08:00","id":1164481,"title":"Do sin-eaters usually go back to their families?","content":"They have no masquerade or veil so they can make contact right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T03:24:15-08:00","id":1164494,"title":"","content":"Most never left their families considering they come back seconds after they die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:11:26-08:00","id":1164571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164494#post1164494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most never left their families considering they come back seconds after they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do they usually tell their family they are a sin eater? How do they come back seconds after they died considering they need time to bargain with a Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:33:32-08:00","id":1164578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164571#post1164571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But do they usually tell their family they are a sin eater? How do they come back seconds after they died considering they need time to bargain with a Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bargain time might not map to real-time.<br /> <br /> As for whether they tell, that depends on a case-by-case basis. &quot;Hi, everyone! I died, but struck a deal with some man-thing made of nails to come back.&quot; What could go wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:39:07-08:00","id":1164579,"title":"","content":"Well probably not literally seconds but it could be minutes, hours, etc, before their ghost is back in their body and anchored by their bargain. They generally return to their lives with no particular obstacles towards readjusting to what they were doing before hand, except for the new found ability to see and hear ghosts and having one that won't go away because it's anchored to you.<br /> <br /> There's no real way in most cases for anyone to tell you're even a Sin-Eater except for other Sin-Eaters, Mages with active death sight and Beasts. Even then it's less of something that pings on their radar, and more of &quot;That guy has a deathly aura around him&quot; for Sin-Eaters and Mages and &quot;That guy smells like he crawled out of the graveyard&quot; to Beasts.<br /> <br /> Really it's up to the Sin-Eater to tell others if they want, that they see dead people now. They'll probably chalk it up to brain damage from lack of oxygen when you temporarily died or that you are just straight up crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:44:48-08:00","id":1164582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164579#post1164579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They'll probably chalk it up to brain damage from lack of oxygen when you temporarily died or that you are just straight up crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be easy to prove, as most of the Sin-Eater powers are fairly flashy. And first edition didn't have people taking Breaking Points upon exposure to the supernatural. You could just introduce them to the geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-02-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:41:47-08:00","id":1164644,"title":"","content":"Well yes you could manifest the geist or use your powers as the most direct way of proving it. Just going by basic trying to normally explain the situation without resorting to it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:06:19-08:00","id":1164677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164582#post1164582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be easy to prove, as most of the Sin-Eater powers are fairly flashy. And first edition didn't have people taking Breaking Points upon exposure to the supernatural. You could just introduce them to the geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>SIn Eater powers are flashy? Like how flashy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:41:02-08:00","id":1164689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164644#post1164644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes you could manifest the geist or use your powers as the most direct way of proving it. Just going by basic trying to normally explain the situation without resorting to it</div> </div> </div> </div>What is manifest the geist do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T17:44:31-08:00","id":1164706,"title":"","content":"The open development blog post for second edition mentions that under certain situations, whether in or out of your control your geist can manifest itself and presumably make itself seen. Not too many details on that so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T18:28:41-08:00","id":1164717,"title":"","content":"As for how flashy Sin-Eater powers are... while we don't know if or how much this could change in 2e, in 1e they could gain access to a wide variety of tricks: several forms of control over elements/emotions/machinery/the senses of others, various forms of shapeshifting, a number of illusion-based powers... things like that. Oh right, and one power to create zombies of increasing potency, and a few powers themed around the creation of elemental homunculi. They did have more subtle tricks as well - many perception-oriented abilities and a range of curses, for example - but in large part if a Sin-Eater dipped into their supernatural side you would <i>know</i> something weird was happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 12-02-2017, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:55:31-08:00","id":1164802,"title":"","content":"Well their power to have their arm detach and move around on its own probably takes the cake for flashiness, maybe shortly followed by their telekinesis of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T11:38:40-08:00","id":1165103,"title":"","content":"Most of the players in my campaign (their characters anyways) did not have families to begin with. Most were distant from them growing up as they could see certain &quot;things&quot; that their family thought them crazy. One of the characters however does have a mother that she is close to. She of course keeps the whole Geist thing at bay, however, the character relationship between them is strong. I think it really depends on the entire background of your character. As far as 'flashy'...again I would think this really depends on how the character behaved prior to their death. As far as powers go, these can get pretty strong ( at least in 1.1) and could definitely make some noise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:33:38-08:00","id":1167679,"title":"","content":"I always thought Industrial Caul was the flashiest: Stick your arm in a machine and your flesh twists to control it, or stick a machine inside your body and then pull it out again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T23:55:42-08:00","id":1170614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164677#post1164677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SIn Eater powers are flashy? Like how flashy?</div> </div> </div> </div>They make D&amp;D spellcasters look low key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T00:09:45-08:00","id":1170616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1170614#post1170614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They make D&amp;D spellcasters look low key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some of the Manifestations. The Curse can be pretty subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:02:48-08:00","id":1171582,"title":"","content":"I think that trying to convince others of your Sin-Eater-ness would require more than flashy powers. Remember that by and large, mortals in Chronicles of Darkness are <i>very</i> willing to explain away whatever they saw as just an illusion, stage-trickery or even just as a hallucination. It's not that they can't see the supernatural effects, it's that they don't <i>want</i> to see it because that shatters so many conventions they think to be true and the implications therein. Integrity breaks are usually from this kind of experience.<br /> <br /> There's also some the fact that by exposing someone to the supernatural, you may very well be causing them a lot more harm than good. Even if your family accepts your strangeness, they don't understand it because they aren't experiencing it - heck, many Sin Eaters probably don't experience the same thing. That lack of understanding can cause a lot of problems as they either misinterpret what you can or can't do, make assumptions as to your true nature (such as thinking you as being a zombie that desires brains) or even as to their own capabilities in dealing with ghosts...or in the worst scenario, try to become like you by their own hand. There is a <i>lot</i> that can go wrong by unveiling yourself and your Geist to your family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T13:53:51-08:00","id":1192050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1164481-do-sin-eaters-usually-go-back-to-their-families?p=1164677#post1164677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SIn Eater powers are flashy? Like how flashy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most were not flashy at all until higher levels. They were invisible to most people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:11:48-08:00","id":1192670,"title":"","content":"Since I run mostly crossovers, we've made the Invictus in charge of the ENTIRE masquerade. It helps since vampires are generally considered to be parasites by the rest of the splats. <br /> <br /> Baring that, no one usually knows the geist died. the heart rate monitor flatlined for half a second, or some such things. Explaining away surviving some pretty horrific injuries is a challege if they want to keep it a secret. So staying with their families, or even returning back to them shouldn't be uncommon. Telling them and making them believe might even happen as well, but consider the risks involved. You are now a monster, thus you put your family at risk since the little pile of seaweed brought you back to life might just take the reigns if your synergy is low enough, AND with these new mechanics, he might just throw a fit. Oh wait, you are now a monster, and hunters are out to put you down, so telling your family or not covering up your miraculus recovery enough might get you with an iron spear to the heart. And if they don't know how to perma kill you, some random person nearby dies when you come back, like your family. Oh wait, aren't you being possessed by a ghost? Won't some Storm Wolves think you are a Claimed and try to do what the hunters did, except better and with more collateral damage?<br /> <br /> It ends up being that the more the geist learns about the new world they were thrust into, the less they would want to return to their family. So initially, yes. After some time, its probably best to keep a lid on it and a safe distance from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}